From 52bd6b4b65f40140f306deefceca7c07914ec210 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:11:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] drm/panfrost: Keep the job interrupts masked during a
 reset

panfrost_reset() masks the job interrupts without setting
PANFROST_COMP_BIT_JOB, so an IRQ thread still running unmasks them
before synchronize_irq() returns. Use panfrost_jm_suspend_irq().

Fixes: 1d0cab5461d7 ("drm/panfrost: Make sure job interrupts are masked before resetting")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20261113-panfrost-long-jobs-v3-0-80ae78d38f6e@gmail.com?part=8
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
index 8ff79ac..d11e9c7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
@@ -707,8 +707,7 @@ panfrost_reset(struct panfrost_device *pfdev,
 	/* Mask job interrupts and synchronize to make sure we won't be
 	 * interrupted during our reset.
 	 */
-	job_write(pfdev, JOB_INT_MASK, 0);
-	synchronize_irq(pfdev->js->irq);
+	panfrost_jm_suspend_irq(pfdev);
 
 	spin_lock(&pfdev->js->job_lock);
 	for (i = 0; i < NUM_JOB_SLOTS; i++) {
-- 
